topics.detail:
AI Art argues that AI art is recognizable. AI Limitations argues that AI tools are not a replacement for knowing what they do. Cooking takes practice and cannot be fully replaced by tech. Non-AI hobby parts are being overshadowed by AI. People need to be informed about AI-generated content.

@michellefranklin.bsky.social: “You know what I had instead of AI when I was a kid? Creative Writer. 50% game, 50% writing tool, It was the greatest software ever. I went to Imaginopolis every damn day and I fucking loved it. I did every single school report with it, and I always got an A.”

AI Art (83.9%) says AI art is recognizable. AI Limitations (16.1%) says AI is not a replacement for human skills.

Game Enjoyment argues that some games are fun despite rough presentation. some games have great storytelling and visuals. games can be worth playing despite technical issues. First TTRPGs argues that My first five TTRPGs set the tone for my gaming style. The order of my first TTRPGs explains my preferences. My first five TTRPGs shaped my gaming experience.

@illiarieka.me: “After 27 hours into Castlevania Belmont’s Curse, I can say I am pleasantly surprised. This was a breath of fresh air after 13 years not having a mainline game. The movement is fluid af, the combat solid, bosses actually feel hard, and the world is fun to explore. Big recommend.”

Game Enjoyment (90.2%) says Games are enjoyable despite flaws. First TTRPGs (9.8%) says People share their first five TTRPGs.

Politics.detail:
Protest Effectiveness argues that Peaceful protests are more effective than violent ones. Protests can influence public opinion and politicians. French Protests argues that Protests are a fundamental right in France. Protests are a fightback against the government.

@english.lemonde.fr: “Second weekend of French protests unfolds without serious incidents: 'The right to protest is just as important as the right to vote'”

Protest Effectiveness (61.8%) says Protests can achieve significant change. French Protests (38.2%) says Protests occur in France.

